\paragraph{Phase segmentation validation.}
The \texttt{<think>} token validation of sparsity-based phase segmentation (\S\ref{sec:background}, Appendix~\ref{app:think-validation}) is limited to a single model (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B) on a single benchmark (GSM8K, $n{=}48$). Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct does not generate explicit reasoning markers, precluding the same validation. Whether the high agreement ($\kappa{=}0.887$) generalizes to other models with explicit CoT delimiters, or to non-mathematical reasoning tasks, remains open.

\paragraph{Mechanism.}
The importance discrimination collapse mechanism is supported by correlational evidence (consistent Gini/CV reduction across all conditions); causal validation through controlled entropy manipulation is needed. The entropy redistribution component replicates on only 2/4 Qwen conditions, suggesting model-specific factors.

